        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. 44% abstention: French local elections 'poorly attended dress rehearsal' for 2027 presidential race France Issued on: 16/03/2026 - 13:29 Modified: 16/03/2026 - 13:35 Following France's lowest voter turnout since the COVID pandemic, Eve Irvine is pleased to welcome Dr. Andrew Smith, Historian of Modern France and Lecturer at Queen Mary University of London. According to Dr. Smith, the defining feature of these municipal elections is not the performance of any single political force. The level of abstention marked the elections more than any other storyline: With roughly 44% of voters staying away, turnout has dropped dramatically compared with earlier decades when participation often exceeded sixty percent and even approached eighty percent in the 1980s. Paris looks at five-way race for new mayor 16/03/2026 France Far-right and left make major gains across France in mayoral election 16/03/2026 France Voter turnout reaches 48.90% in France's first round of local elections 15/03/2026 France Ukraine recovering from Russian strike, concerned Putin is benefiting from Iran war 15/03/2026 Europe French parties test strategies in municipal elections ahead of 2027 presidential poll 15/03/2026 France Made in UK: Ukrainian drone company to open first UK plant to boost production 13/03/2026 Europe Strait of Hormuz: Iran leverages control of a critical chokepoint in the global oil trade 13/03/2026 Middle East 'European Union needs a bit of a revolution: There is no European strategy or foreign policy' 12/03/2026 Europe Bodies of anonymous migrants wash up in Sicily weeks after cyclone 11/03/2026 Europe"
