        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Trump presses China, says NATO faces 'very bad' future if allies don't help open Hormuz Strait Middle East Issued on: 16/03/2026 - 13:25 US President Donald Trump on Sunday sought to pressure NATO allies and China to help reopen the Strait of Hormuz, the critical oil transport conduit that Iran has effectively closed in retaliation for the US and Israeli war against Tehran. Global oil prices have surged by 40 to 50 percent as Iran has choked off the waterway and attacked energy and shipping industry targets among its Gulf neighbours. 16/03/2026 Middle East UK won't commit soldiers to a war without 'legal basis' amid Trump threats 16/03/2026 Middle East Israeli forces kill four in a car in West Bank 16/03/2026 Middle East Answering Trump's call for help in Middle East 'political suicide' for allies 16/03/2026 Middle East IDF launches 'limited operation' in Lebanon as 'buffer zone expands significantly' 16/03/2026 Middle East Israel pounds Beirut's southern suburbs with death toll raising to 850 16/03/2026 Middle East Trump calls for help on securing Strait of Hormuz as oil prices surge 16/03/2026 Middle East Gulf States still under Iranian fire as Trump boasts of successful US strikes 16/03/2026 Middle East Severe sandstorm sweeps through Gaza tent camps 15/03/2026 Middle East"
